From: Ygbs <h@ypixel.net>
Subject: Embedded WebSocket Proxy for minetest-wasm browser clients

Description:
  Adds an embedded µWS WebSocket proxy server to Luanti, allowing
  minetest-wasm browser clients to connect via WebSocket instead of
  raw UDP.  The proxy injects raw MTP packets into the existing
  ConnectionReceiveThread via a shared queue — no UDP loopback,
  no MTP protocol modification.

  Features:
  - X-Forwarded-For real IP extraction (Cloudflare/Nginx compatible)
  - IPv6 support (IPv4-mapped ::ffff: addresses handled correctly)
  - Virtual port assignment per WS session (multiple browser tabs
    from the same IP work correctly, each gets a unique MTP peer)
  - Fake DNS resolver (returns ws_dns_ip for all lookups)
  - Graceful shutdown (Loop::defer + join, no detach/UAF)

  Applies to:  Luanti 5.16.1 (tag: 5ebd9b5)
  Repository:  https://github.com/luanti-org/luanti
  Based on 5 squashed commits:
    3704ee5 ws_proxy: fix stop() — use Loop::defer()+join() instead of detach()
358046a ws_proxy: virtual ports for multi-client same-IP support
8e5ee0a ws_proxy: handle IPv6 X-Forwarded-For addresses
60000eb ws_proxy: shared-queue direct injection (no UDP loopback)
404bd22 feat: embed WebSocket proxy (uWebSockets) for minetest-wasm browser clients

Usage — apply the patch:
  git clone https://github.com/luanti-org/luanti
  cd luanti
  git checkout 5.16.1

  # Clone uWebSockets next to the luanti source tree
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/uNetworking/uWebSockets.git ../uWebSockets

  git apply /path/to/ws_proxy.patch

Build — server only:
  mkdir build && cd build
  cmake .. -DBUILD_SERVER=ON -DBUILD_CLIENT=OFF -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  make -j$(nproc)
  # Binary: bin/luantiserver

Build — with LuaJIT (recommended for VoxeLibre):
  cmake .. -DBUILD_SERVER=ON -DBUILD_CLIENT=OFF -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
    -DENABLE_LUAJIT=ON
  make -j$(nproc)

Configuration (minetest.conf):
  ws_port = 8888          # 0 = disable WebSocket proxy
  ws_bind_address =        # empty = 0.0.0.0 (bind all interfaces)
  ws_dns_ip = 1.1.1.1     # fake DNS response for browser client

  # Optional: reduce packet-quota log noise during initial world sync
  max_packets_per_iteration = 4096

Proxy setup (Nginx example for WSS termination):
  location /mtproxy {
      proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8888;
      proxy_http_version 1.1;
      proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
      proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
      proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
      proxy_read_timeout 86400s;
      proxy_send_timeout 86400s;
  }

Files changed (9 files, +596/-8):
  src/CMakeLists.txt          — uSockets static lib + ws_proxy.cpp target
  src/defaultsettings.cpp     — ws_port/ws_bind_address/ws_dns_ip defaults
  src/network/mtp/impl.h      — WsProxy forward-declare + setWsProxy/getWsProxy
  src/network/mtp/threads.cpp — WS inject in receive(), WS route in rawSend()
  src/network/socket.h        — getFamily() for IPv6 check
  src/network/ws_proxy.cpp    — µWS event loop, queues, PROXY handshake (NEW)
  src/network/ws_proxy.h      — WsProxy class interface (NEW)
  src/server.cpp              — start/stop WsProxy in Server::start()
  src/server.h                — WsProxy unique_ptr member

